 # Progressive and Multi-stage Training
 
-Also called: Multi-stage Optimization, Curriculum Training for Gaussians, Progressive Densification
+Also called: Multi-stage Optimization, Coarse-to-Fine Training, Curriculum Learning for 3DGS
 
 ## Overview
-Progressive and Multi-stage Training refers to a family of optimization strategies for 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) that decompose the reconstruction process into distinct phases or stages rather than optimizing the primitive set in a single continuous pass [S1, unofficial]. This approach solves the problem of converging to local minima, producing blurry details, or suffering from optimization instability that often results from single-stage training of sparse primitives [S1, unofficial]. By alternating between coarse initialization, global structural guidance, and fine-grained densification, these methods yield significantly higher rendering quality and stability than single-stage baselines [S1, unofficial].
+Progressive and Multi-stage Training refers to optimization strategies that decompose the training of 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) into distinct phases or stages, rather than optimizing the primitive set in a single continuous pass [S1, unofficial]. This approach solves the problem of converging to local minima, producing blurry details, or suffering from instability that often results from single-stage training of sparse primitives [S1, unofficial]. By alternating between coarse initialization and fine-grained densification, or by decoupling geometry and pose learning, it yields significantly higher rendering quality and stability than single-stage baselines [S1, unofficial].
 
